description: Design system rules for all Flutter UI implementation

# Design System

## Purpose

This project uses a centralized Design System.
The Design System is the single source of truth for all visual elements.
Every screen, widget and component must follow these rules.
Never create your own visual styles if an existing token already exists.

# Source Files
All design tokens are located under:

lib/core/theme/
Files:

- app_theme.dart
- app_colors.dart
- app_typography.dart
- app_spacing.dart
- app_radius.dart
- app_shadows.dart
- app_sized.dart
- app_responsive.dart
- extensions/theme_extensions.dart
- extensions/responsive_extensions.dart

The implementation must always reuse these files.

# Colors

DO
- Use AppColors
- Use ThemeExtension
- Use ColorScheme when provided
DON'T
- Never use Color(...)
- Never use hexadecimal colors directly
- Never create temporary colors inside widgets

# Typography

DO
- Use AppTypography
- Reuse predefined text styles

DON'T
- Never create TextStyle inline
- Never hardcode font size
- Never hardcode font weight

AppTypography.bodyMedium ✔ 

TextStyle(
  fontSize: 15,
  fontWeight: FontWeight.w600,
)✘

# Spacing
Use AppSpacing for every spacing value.
DO
AppSpacing.xs
AppSpacing.sm
AppSpacing.md
AppSpacing.lg
AppSpacing.xl

DON'T
SizedBox(height: 17)
Padding(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(13),
)

# Radius
Always use AppRadius.

Never write
BorderRadius.circular(14)

Use
AppRadius.md

# Shadows
Always use AppShadows.
Never create BoxShadow manually unless a new design token is added.

# Sizes
Use AppSized whenever fixed component sizes already exist.
Avoid magic numbers.


# Responsive

Always use the project's responsive utilities.
Never calculate screen sizes manually if an existing helper exists.
Reuse:
- AppResponsive
- Responsive Extensions

# Theme
The application supports Light and Dark themes.
Never check theme manually using arbitrary conditions.
Always obtain colors from Theme or Theme Extensions.

# Widget
Before creating a new widget:

1. Search existing global widget in this path : keyva\lib\core\widget
2. Reuse existing components whenever possible.
3. Only create a new reusable component if none exists.
Avoid duplicated UI.

Reusable UI widget:
lib/core/widget/

Feature specific widgets:
lib/features/{feature}/widgets/


Rules:

- Generic widgets belong to core/widget.
- Feature widgets must stay inside their feature.
- Never create UI components inside controllers or views.

# assets

Use the project's assets dirctory.
assets must have consistent sizes.
Never hardcode assets sizes if a design token exists.

Icons path :keyva\assets\icons
Fonts path :keyva\assets\fonts
Iamges path :keyva\assets\iamges
Illustrations path :keyva\assets\iamges\illustrations

# Animations
Keep animations subtle.
Reuse existing animation durations and curves.
Avoid custom animation values unless necessary.

# Accessibility
Every interactive widget should:
- have sufficient touch target
- support dark mode
- support text scaling
- use semantic widgets where appropriate

# Layout

Use consistent spacing.
Do not align widgets by trial and error.
Build layouts using:
- Row
- Column
- Expanded
- Flexible
- Spacer
Avoid unnecessary nested widgets.


# Hardcoded Values

The following are forbidden unless explicitly approved.
- Colors
- Font sizes
- Border radius
- Spacing
- Shadow values
- Durations
- Opacity values
Always use existing design tokens.

# Before Writing UI

Before implementing any screen:

1. Read the design system.
2. Search reusable components.
3. Use existing design tokens.
4. Keep the implementation consistent with the rest of the application.

If any rule conflicts with existing code, prefer the Design System.
If documentation is unclear, ask before making assumptions.

# MVVM UI Rules

View:
- Only responsible for UI rendering.
- No business logic.
- No data processing.

Controller/ViewModel:
- Handles state.
- Handles UI logic.
- Exposes observable states.

widget : 
- Feature specific widgets


Never:
- call repositories directly from widgets.
- write business logic inside build().

